    <div id="ilrsu">
      <section class="text_gray_six_hundred body-font">
        <div class="container_base margin_x_auto flexbox_container padding_x_five padding_y_twenty_four medium_flex_direction_row flex_direction_column items_center_position">
          <div class="large_max_width_large large_width_full medium_width_half width_five_sixth margin_bottom_ten medium_margin_bottom_zero">
            <img class="object_cover_style object_center_style border_rounded" alt="feature" src="img/860d75ebfc0e47b118dde5d8e9fe3d01.jpg" />
          </div>
          <div class="large_flex_growth medium_width_half large_padding_left_twenty_four medium_padding_left_sixteen flexbox_container flex_direction_column medium_items_start medium_text_direction_left items_center_position text_direction_center">
            <h1 class="title-font small_text_size_three_extra_large text_size_two_extra_large margin_bottom_four font_weight_medium text_gray_nine_hundred">A considered approach to interior design</h1>
            <p class="margin_bottom_eight line_height_relaxed">
              Good interior design is more than selecting attractive finishes. It considers the relationship between a room’s proportions, its daily uses and the atmosphere its occupants want to create. Maison North Design’s approach gives attention to those connected decisions, from the overall layout and palette to the materials and details that bring a scheme together. The aim is to make the design process clear and personal, while keeping each choice relevant to the home and the people who
              live there.
            </p>
            <div class="grid_layout medium_grid_columns_double gap_six">
              <div class="flexbox_container flex_direction_column items_start_position text_direction_left">
                <h2 class="text_size_large font_weight_medium text_gray_nine_hundred margin_bottom_two">Designed around everyday life</h2>
                <p class="line_height_relaxed text_size_base">
                  A home should support the routines and activities that take place within it. Thinking about how each room is used can help guide decisions about layout, furniture, storage and lighting before decorative details are settled. This practical starting point makes it easier to create interiors that feel natural to move through and comfortable to spend time in. The result is not a prescribed style, but a considered design direction shaped by the household’s needs, preferences and the
                  character of the property.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="flexbox_container flex_direction_column items_start_position text_direction_left">
                <h2 class="text_size_large font_weight_medium text_gray_nine_hundred margin_bottom_two">A cohesive material palette</h2>
                <p class="line_height_relaxed text_size_base">
                  Colours, finishes and textures influence how a space feels and how its different elements relate to one another. A carefully considered palette can bring a sense of continuity across rooms while still allowing each area to have its own character. Looking at materials together, rather than in isolation, helps clarify which combinations feel balanced within a particular home. The process can take account of existing features and personal taste, creating a design direction that
                  feels connected to the property rather than borrowed from a passing trend.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="flexbox_container flex_direction_column items_start_position text_direction_left">
                <h2 class="text_size_large font_weight_medium text_gray_nine_hundred margin_bottom_two">Attention to light and proportion</h2>
                <p class="line_height_relaxed text_size_base">
                  Light and scale have a strong effect on the experience of an interior. Considering a room’s proportions, natural light and existing architectural details can inform choices about layout, colour, furnishings and artificial lighting. These elements are most effective when planned as part of the same conversation, so that the design feels harmonious throughout the day and across different uses of the room. Careful attention to these fundamentals helps create interiors that feel
                  balanced without making unsupported promises about how a particular space will perform.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="flexbox_container flex_direction_column items_start_position text_direction_left">
                <h2 class="text_size_large font_weight_medium text_gray_nine_hundred margin_bottom_two">A clear design conversation</h2>
                <p class="line_height_relaxed text_size_base">
                  A thoughtful project begins with an open discussion about what matters to the people who will use the space. Priorities, preferences and practical considerations can be explored before design directions are developed, helping keep decisions grounded in the home and its occupants. Clear communication also gives clients an opportunity to ask questions and consider options as the design takes shape. Every property and brief is different, so the process should leave room for
                  individual needs rather than assume that one solution will suit everyone.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
