              <p class="margin_top_six text_size_large line_height_eight text_gray_six_hundred">Interior design brings together practical and visual decisions. The layout, light, materials, colour and furnishings all influence how a home feels and functions. Considering these elements in relation to one another can help establish a coherent direction that reflects both the property and the people who live there.</p>
              <p class="margin_top_six text_size_large line_height_eight text_gray_six_hundred">
                There is no single formula for a successful interior, and no set of figures can describe the experience of every home. These four numbered themes are design considerations, not company performance statistics or claims about completed projects. They offer a simple way to explore the conversations that can shape an interior design brief, from understanding how a space is used to choosing details that feel personal and appropriate.
              </p>
