            <h2 class="text_size_two_extra_large font_weight_bold line_height_ten letter_spacing_tight text_gray_nine_hundred">Frequently asked questions</h2>
            <p class="margin_top_six text_size_base line_height_seven text_gray_six_hundred">Every home and design brief is different, so the answers below offer general guidance rather than promises about a particular project. If you have a question about an interior design enquiry, share the details that feel relevant and the next steps can be discussed directly.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="margin_top_twenty">
            <dl class="space_y_sixteen small_grid small_grid_columns_double small_gap_x_six small_gap_y_sixteen small_space_y_zero large_gap_x_ten">
              <div>
                <dt class="text_size_base font_weight_semibold line_height_seven text_gray_nine_hundred">What does interior design consider?</dt>
                <dd class="margin_top_two text_size_base line_height_seven text_gray_six_hundred">Interior design can consider how rooms are used, how spaces connect, and how elements such as layout, lighting, colour, materials and furnishings work together. The appropriate focus depends on the property and the brief.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt class="text_size_base font_weight_semibold line_height_seven text_gray_nine_hundred">Can I share my own ideas and preferences?</dt>
                <dd class="margin_top_two text_size_base line_height_seven text_gray_six_hundred">Yes. Your preferences, routines and practical priorities are useful starting points for a design conversation. Sharing inspiration or describing what does and does not feel right can help clarify the direction you want to explore.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt class="text_size_base font_weight_semibold line_height_seven text_gray_nine_hundred">Do you work with homes across England?</dt>
